  "notes": "Source: official City College of New York (Grove School of Engineering) Computer Science Curriculum Sheet, 8-semester grid, dated July 6, 2023, 'Fall 2023 - Spring 2024': https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/sites/default/files/2024-03/csc-curric-2023-2024--2023-07-06.pdf. Transcribed 2026-09-30 from the PDF text layer; semester layout, course codes, titles, credits, and per-course prerequisites copied from the sheet. Course codes normalized to 'CSC 10300' style (the sheet prints 'CSc 10300'; the official catalog uses 'CSC 10300'). catalog_year '2023-2024' is the honest source year: no newer CSc curriculum sheet is published as of 2026-09-30 (Civil and Mechanical Engineering have 2026-2027 sheets; Computer Science does not). Cross-checks: (1) the official CUNY Academic Undergraduate Report, City College, October 2021 (cuny.edu) confirms program course titles/credits and the 127-credit degree total; (2) the official CpE 2023-2024 curriculum sheet and its prerequisite flowchart confirm the shared-course prerequisite chains (CSC 33200 requires CSC 22000 & CSC 22100; CSC 34200 requires (CSC 21000 & EE 21000) or CSC 21100, with corequisite CSC 34300); (3) the official CSC 113 syllabus page (ccny.cuny.edu/compsci/csc-113-syllabus) confirms CSC 11300's prerequisite is CSC 10300. Caveats: (a) sheet footnote 1: the latest curriculum sheet supersedes any curriculum or pre-/corequisite information in the Undergraduate Bulletin or online; (b) 'or permission' alternatives on the sheet are not course codes and are documented here, not in prereqs; (c) the sheet lists FIQWS as an alternative prerequisite for ENGL 21007 and '2100x' as an alternative for CSC 22100 - neither is a standard course code, so only ENGL 11000 and ENGL 21007 appear in prereqs; (d) the sheet lists CSC 34200 and CSC 34300 as corequisites of each other; both are sequenced in the same semester here, with the lab (34300) shown depending on the lecture (34200); (e) CSC 59866 requires senior standing and permission (not a course code); (f) MATH 19500 is the placement-level prerequisite the sheet names for MATH 20100 and CSC 10300; (g) sheet titles abbreviated for layout (e.g. 'Fund.', 'Probability & Statistics for Computer Sci') were expanded using the official CUNY October 2021 report wording; elective A/B/C option titles are quoted verbatim as printed on the sheet, including abbreviations.",
